    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>83</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of ethylene glycol dissolved in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>625</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of water. The freezing point of the solution is ..... K. (Nearest integer)<br />[Use : Molal Freezing point depression constant of water <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>86</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math><br />Freezing point of water <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>273</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math><br />Atomic masses : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mo>]</mo></math>",
